  "starter_code": "class Solution {\n    public int[] moveZeroes(int[] nums) {\n        // TODO: write your solution here\n        return new int[0];\n    }\n}\n",
  "hints": [
    "Think about where the next non-zero value should go.",
    "Keep a write index. Copy each non-zero value to that index and advance it; fill the rest with zeroes.",
    "w = 0\nfor n in nums:\n    if n != 0: nums[w] = n; w += 1\nwhile w < len(nums): nums[w] = 0; w += 1\nreturn nums",
    "The write pointer never passes the read pointer, so this works in place in one pass: O(n) time, O(1) extra space. Order is kept because values are written in the order they're read."
  ],
  "expected_complexity": {
    "time": "O(n)",
    "space": "O(1)"
  },
